      "research_question": "How should international health authorities and tournament hosts formulate travel health strategies when a major global sporting event coincides with an emerging viral crisis lacking approved medical countermeasures?",
      "study_design": "This publication is a peer-reviewed journal article that presents a policy perspective and strategic recommendation rather than an empirical clinical or observational study.",
      "population_setting": "The analysis targets international travelers and attendees participating in large-scale cross-border mass gatherings.",
      "main_findings": "Existing host country measures, such as border restrictions and prolonged isolation mandates, lack strong epidemiological backing. The authors emphasize that standardized, risk-appropriate travel health frameworks are critically needed for future pandemic-era mega-events.",
      "public_health_relevance": "The discussion identifies operational gaps in managing transmissible disease threats during high-density international tourism and sports tournaments.",
